cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "Interpretable Deep Reinforcement Learning for Element-level Bridge Life-cycle Optimization (code)"
abstract: >-
  Research code accompanying Moayyedi & Yang (2026). An interpretable deep
  reinforcement learning framework for risk-based, element-level bridge
  life-cycle optimization under the 2022 SNBI element-level condition-state
  specification. Includes a custom Gymnasium/TorchRL bridge-management
  environment, PPO actor-critic training with differentiable soft-tree actors
  distilled into compact oblique decision trees via temperature annealing and
  regularization-based pruning, dynamic-programming baselines, and MLE/method-of-
  moments fitting of the initial condition-state distribution from FHWA
  InfoBridge inspection data.
type: software
